{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ECS"}],"role":"article","title":"Getting Started with ECS","roleHeading":"Article"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS\/GettingStarted","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Define components, spawn entities, and move them with systems that run in a schedule and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"simulation."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In an entity component system, the things your program tracks are "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"entities","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": plain handles that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own nothing themselves. The data lives in "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"components","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", small value types attached to entities,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such as a position or a health bar. The behavior lives in "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"systems","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", functions that run over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every entity holding a particular set of components. A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"world"}]},{"type":"text","text":" holds the entities and their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"components, and a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"schedule","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" runs systems on it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This article builds a tiny game step by step: balls that move, and that disappear when their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"health runs out.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Define-Components","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Define Components"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A component is a value type that conforms to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Component","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". It needs no other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requirements; a struct with stored properties is enough. A component can also be empty, to mark","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the entities that have it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The following components describe where an entity is, how fast it moves, and how much health it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["struct Position: Component { var x: Double, y: Double }","struct Velocity: Component { var dx: Double, dy: Double }","struct Health: Component { var current: Int }"],"syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Spawn-Entities","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Spawn Entities"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World"},{"type":"text","text":" holds entities and their components. Create an empty world, then call"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spawn(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" with the components a new entity starts with. Spawning returns an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity"},{"type":"text","text":", the handle you use to read and change that entity later:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 2))","let rock = world.spawn(Position(x: 5, y: 5))","print(world.count)","\/\/ Prints \"2\"","","world[Position.self, of: ball].x = 10","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 10.0, y: 0.0)\"","","world.insert(Health(current: 3), into: rock)","print(world.contains(Health.self, in: rock))","\/\/ Prints \"true\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The subscript reads one component of one entity, and changes it in place when you assign through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. Use "},{"code":"insert(_:into:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to add a component to an entity, "},{"code":"remove(_:from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to take one away,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"code":"despawn(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to remove the entity and all of its components."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A world is a value: assigning it to another variable makes an independent copy, and the two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"share their storage until one of them changes.","type":"text"}]},{"name":"Important","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Like an array subscript, the subscript traps if the entity doesn’t hold the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component, or has been despawned. Each such operation has a "},{"code":"checked","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" spelling, such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"world[checked: Position.self, of: ball]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", that throws an error instead."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"important"},{"anchor":"Query-and-Update-Many-Entities","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Query and Update Many Entities"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A query visits every entity holding a set of component types. Call ","type":"text"},{"code":"query(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with the types,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and iterate over the result; each row holds the entity followed by its components. Narrow a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"query with ","type":"text"},{"code":"with(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"without(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 2))","world.spawn(Position(x: 5, y: 5))","","for (_, position) in world.query(Position.self).without(Velocity.self) {","    print(position)  \/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 5.0, y: 5.0)\"","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To change components across many entities, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"update(_:reading:body:)"},{"type":"text","text":". It visits every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entity holding the written type and the read types, and passes the written component "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"along with a row of the others. This is the fastest way to change many entities:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 2))","let rock = world.spawn(Position(x: 5, y: 5))","","world.update(Position.self, reading: Velocity.self) { position, row in","    position.x += row.components.dx","    position.y += row.components.dy","}","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 2.0)\"","print(world[Position.self, of: rock])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 5.0, y: 5.0)\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The rock has no velocity, so the update skips it."}]},{"anchor":"Write-Systems","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Write Systems"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A system is a rule your program applies over and over, such as moving everything that has a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"velocity. Declare one with the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" macro on a type with a "},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"types of the method’s parameters say what the system reads and writes:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" writes components, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" reads them, and an "},{"code":"inout","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" records spawns and despawns to apply once the system, and the systems"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"running alongside it, finish."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following systems move each entity by its velocity, and despawn each entity whose health has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run out:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["@System","struct Movement {","    func run(_ movers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>) {","        movers { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx","            position.y += row.components.dy","        }","    }","}","","@System","struct Reaper {","    func run(_ living: Query<Health>, commands: inout Commands) {","        for (entity, health) in living where health.current <= 0 {","            commands.despawn(entity)","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because a system states what it touches, a schedule knows which systems can run at the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"time. Two parameters that name the same component, one of them writing it, such as two updates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of "},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", are a compile-time error."}]},{"anchor":"Run-a-Schedule","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Run a Schedule"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule"},{"type":"text","text":" runs systems in the order you write them. Call"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to run every system once on a world:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 2), Health(current: 3))","let ghost = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Health(current: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Movement()","    Reaper()","}","frame.run(on: &world)","","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 2.0)\"","print(world.contains(ghost))","\/\/ Prints \"false\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems that don’t conflict, like these two, run at the same time. Neither reads what the other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writes, so the result doesn’t depend on which runs first, and the commands they record apply once"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"both finish. To order systems differently, add"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a constraint such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Reaper().after(Movement.self)"},{"type":"text","text":", and to skip a system unless a condition"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holds, add "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"runIf(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"Run-a-Simulation","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Run a Simulation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A game or simulation runs its systems every frame. A "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation"},{"type":"text","text":" owns a world"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and schedules named by label, and you call "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation\/update(elapsed:)"},{"type":"text","text":" once a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"frame with the time that passed. Systems added to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/fixedUpdate"},{"type":"text","text":" label run once for every fixed timestep of that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"time, so they advance at the same rate however long each frame takes:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 2), Health(current: 3))","","var simulation = Simulation(world, fixedTimestep: .milliseconds(10))","simulation.add(to: .fixedUpdate) { Movement() }","simulation.add(to: .update) { Reaper() }","","simulation.update(elapsed: .milliseconds(30))","print(simulation.world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 3.0, y: 6.0)\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The 30-millisecond frame covers three timesteps, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Movement"},{"type":"text","text":" runs three times. Because it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"moves each entity by its velocity once a run, the velocity here is a distance per timestep. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system that needs the length of a step reads the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/FixedTime","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" resource, and one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that needs the length of a frame reads "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Time","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"Next-Steps","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Next Steps"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Learn about the world in depth, including bundles, relations, hierarchies, events and change","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"detection, in ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn about system parameters, ordering and system sets in "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn about states and the order of a frame in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ecs\/gettingstarted"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/Simulation":{"url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/simulation","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Simulation"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A world and its schedules by label, advanced one frame at a time."}],"title":"Simulation","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Simulation"}]},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Component":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Component","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/component","title":"Component","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that can be stored as a component of an entity."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Component"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Component"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule":{"url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a world frame by frame, with schedules for startup, a fixed timestep and each frame, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with states that switch systems on and off."}],"title":"SimulationModule","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/Time":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Time","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/time","title":"Time","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A resource holding the time a simulation has advanced."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Time","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Time","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems","title":"Systems","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","title":"Schedule","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel/fixedUpdate":{"url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel\/fixedupdate","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fixedUpdate","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScheduleLabel","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SimulationModule13ScheduleLabelV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"fixedUpdate","abstract":[{"text":"The label of the schedule that runs once for each fixed timestep of elapsed time.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/fixedUpdate"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Query":{"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/query","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Query","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Query","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A description of the entities to visit and the components to read from each.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Query","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Update":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Update","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that changes a component of every entity that holds it.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Update","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/update","title":"Update","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/run(on:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/run(on:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"run","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"on","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V","text":"World","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"title":"run(on:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs each system once on a world, running systems that don’t depend on each other at the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same time."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)"},"doc://ECS/documentation/ECS":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build games and simulations from entities, the components they hold, and systems that update"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them in a declared order."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ecs","title":"ECS","identifier":"doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule":{"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule","abstract":[{"text":"Store the state of a game or simulation as entities and components, and read and change it with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"queries, updates, and commands.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"WorldModule","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/FixedTime":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"FixedTime"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A resource holding the fixed timestep of a simulation."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"FixedTime"}],"url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/fixedtime","title":"FixedTime","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/FixedTime"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Entity":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/entity","title":"Entity","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A handle that identifies one entity in a world."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Entity","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Entity","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World":{"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"World"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A collection of entities, the components they hold, and resources."}],"title":"World","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"World"}]},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/Simulation/update(elapsed:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation\/update(elapsed:)","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/simulation\/update(elapsed:)","title":"update(elapsed:)","abstract":[{"text":"Advances the simulation by one frame.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"update","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"elapsed","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","text":"Duration","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Commands":{"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/commands","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Commands","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"Commands","abstract":[{"text":"A buffer of changes to a world, recorded now and applied later in the order they were","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"recorded.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Commands","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system()","title":"System()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Makes a type a system whose access comes from the parameters of its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method."}],"fragments":[{"text":"macro","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"System","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"}}}